-- Every mile the plan asks for is in the plan

-- prescribed_distance now means the expected TOTAL SESSION DISTANCE. The
-- components describe the work inside it. That one ruling resolves three
-- undercounts that had been compounding since the block was authored:
--
--   The warm-up and cool-down. Typed on three Tuesdays out of forty-five
--   sessions, run on all of them. Jose's 3 x 2 mi came back at 9.09 miles
--   against an authored 6, and that week is one of the few that has them.
--
--   The named sessions. Hills + strides types eight twelve-second hills and
--   four twenty-second strides -- three minutes of running -- and declares five
--   miles. The five was right and the inside was never written down.
--
--   The recoveries. recovery_seconds and recovery_kind have always been on the
--   row and nothing has ever counted them. A jog, float or easy recovery is
--   running: the four jogs inside 5 x 3 min are 1.14 miles. A standing recovery
--   is not, and stays uncounted.
--
-- No hard piece changes anywhere in this. One long run changes: W12's Saturday
-- goes from 8 + 4 at race pace to 12 + 4, making it the block's longest and the
-- week its aerobic peak. The four miles at race pace are untouched -- the
-- purpose of that week is volume, not more specificity.
--
-- Then the easy days. Monday, Wednesday and Friday are authored for W3 through
-- W13 as a smooth aerobic progression -- 21, 22, 23, 24, 23, 24, 25, 26, 24, 30,
-- 26 -- while the weekly total is left to breathe around the key sessions:
--
--   43 . 48 . 54 . 50 . 39 . 46 . 52 . 53 . 48 . 58 . 50
--
-- W7 stays the major cutback, but the cutback is made by withdrawing the
-- structured load, not by starving the aerobic base a fortnight before the
-- ownership progression. Sunday is rest.
--
-- The weekly `Across the week` budget rows are deliberately NOT deleted. They
-- are the audit layer for this migration and the record of how the easy running
-- was authored before it had days. The surfaces stop counting a budget in a week
-- that has authored easy days.
--
-- Nothing here is written directly. Every change goes through revise_session and
-- author_session, so each one carries its reason, its version number and its
-- author. The session's whole history stays legible.
--
-- Two sessions could not keep their declared total, and both are named on the
-- record rather than quietly rounded:
--
--   The Wave declares 6 and needs 7.23 once a real warm-up sits in front of
--   twenty minutes at 6:25-6:30.
--   The Governor declares 5 and needs 6.94 for the same reason, plus its five
--   ninety-second jogs.
--
-- W14 and W15 are untouched. The taper and race week are a coaching decision,
-- not a mileage one.

